# FABLE-SONNET-CALLABLE-PRIORITY-20260923-130 negative (closes plan :213,
# :216). `bar` is callable and takes NO argument. `bar: 5` (colon form with
# a body) resolves bar as callable first -- per the universal priority, a
# callable head is ALWAYS a call, never a fallback to assignment -- so the
# refusal must be a CALL-signature error ("incompatible entry signature"),
# never "assignment target must be a declared typed mutable value". That
# second wording would mean the translator tried assignment as a fallback
# after call resolution somehow failed silently, which the priority rule
# forbids: an unusable call is a call error, with no fallback path at all.
fn: bar () int
    return: 0
end: bar

bar: 5
return: 0
